    "title": "VIDEO: No. 18 Rambelles conclude nonconference schedule with road trip in Colorado's high altitude - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Griff McClellan ,\n5 hours ago\nSAN ANGELO, Texas ( Concho Valley Homepage ) — Click the video above to preview Angelo State soccer’s remaining nonconference schedule, beginning Thursday, Sept. 11.\nThe No. 18 Angelo State Rambelles still search for the team’s first win of the 2025 season. The Rambelles opened the new season last week with a two-game homestand, recording a loss and tie versus opponents No. 4 Colorado School of Mines and Oklahoma Baptist, respectively.\nAngelo State’s next two opponents are Colorado State University Pueblo and Metropolitan State University of Denver, with matches scheduled on Thursday, Sept. 11 and Saturday, Sept. 13, respectively. A two-game road trip in Colorado inevitably means high altitude will be a factor. The Rambelles have a challenge ahead of itself, but the team is ready for it in the vision of assistant coach Harold Muñoz.\n“The altitude takes a toll,” Muñoz said. “Obviously our girls are in pretty good shape and we should be up for the task. But [the altitude] does take a toll on your body whenever you have to run long distances.”\nAngelo State’s first matchup at CSU Pueblo kicks off at 7 p.m. on Thursday, Sept. 11.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ConchoValleyHomepage.com.",
